--TEST--
`Sheet::column` before the first data row throws naming the sheet, also when the `columns` option gives the key, and after the first row it returns the data rows without the header row: rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-roster
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Sheet::column
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Workbook;

var $book = Workbook::createInMemory();
var $orders = $book->sheet("Orders", {columns: ["order" => {header: "Order"}, "total" => {header: "Total"}]});
try {
    echo $orders->column("total"), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// A column letter has no data row either.
try {
    echo $orders->column("B"), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

$orders->add(["order" => 1042, "total" => 19.5]);
echo $orders->column("total"), "\n";
$orders->add(["order" => 1043, "total" => 5.0]);
echo $orders->column("B"), "\n";
$book->finish();
--EXPECT--
The sheet `Orders` has no data row yet. Call `column` after you add the first row.
The sheet `Orders` has no data row yet. Call `column` after you add the first row.
B2:B2
B2:B3
